---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro'
import FinalCTA from '../components/blocks/CTA/FinalCTA.astro'

const SEO = {
	title: 'WordPress AI Editing for Marketing Teams | Frontman Features',
	description:
		'Change marketing copy, Gutenberg blocks, Elementor sections, and navigation on your existing WordPress site. Describe the result instead of learning every editor control.'
}
---

<Layout title={SEO.title} description={SEO.description}>
	<section class="bg-neutral-950 px-6 pb-16 pt-24 text-white md:pt-32">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Your marketing ideas.<br />Your WordPress site.<br />Make the changes yourself.</h1>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">You know the message, the campaign, and what the page needs. Frontman turns your requests into WordPress edits—without an agency handoff for every headline or section.</p>
			<Button size="lg" style="primary" link="https://wordpress.org/plugins/frontman-agentic-ai-editor/" classes="mt-8">Get Frontman for WordPress</Button>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-neutral-300">Administrator access, Frontman service access, and your own AI provider are required. <a href="/pricing/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">See pricing and separate AI costs</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-white px-6 py-16 text-neutral-950 md:py-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Keep the site. Change the story.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">Frontman installs into your existing WordPress site. Keep your CMS, content, and publishing workflow instead of migrating to another website builder.</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">Work with Gutenberg blocks and Elementor pages. Frontman also has tools for navigation, templates, widgets, and WooCommerce when active. <a href="/docs/integrations/wordpress/#what-the-agent-can-do" class="copy-link text-violet-800 underline underline-offset-4">See supported tools and compatibility details</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-neutral-950 px-6 py-16 text-white md:py-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-12">
			<div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Campaign copy that keeps up.</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Replace a stale headline, clarify a CTA, or update a page for your next campaign. Describe the message you want and inspect the result on the page.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Rework the section, not your whole setup.</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Add, move, or update Gutenberg blocks and Elementor elements. Ask for changes to content, spacing, or layout without finding every page-builder control yourself.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Give the next campaign a place to land.</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Create or update a page, then add its navigation link. Keep the work inside the WordPress site your team already maintains.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Judge the result where your visitors see it.</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Chat sits beside the site preview. Select an element to clarify your request, inspect the changed page, and ask for another pass. Check mobile layouts before you call the work finished.</p>
				<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-neutral-300">Preview is not an approval gate. Changes to published content on a live installation can go live immediately.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-white px-6 py-16 text-neutral-950 md:py-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">A marketing lead took the redesign into his own hands.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">AutonomyAI's Guy Leshno had no prior WordPress experience. He reported redesigning its existing Elementor site in roughly two weeks of part-time work, including stakeholder feedback.</p>
			<blockquote class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold leading-relaxed">“Without Frontman, I would never have been able to accomplish this task by myself.”</blockquote>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base text-neutral-600">Guy Leshno · Marketing Lead, AutonomyAI</p>
			<a href="/blog/autonomyai-wordpress-redesign-case-study/" class="copy-link mt-6 inline-block font-semibold text-violet-800 underline underline-offset-4">Read the customer story and see the before and after</a>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-neutral-600">Customer-reported result in a Frontman-authored case study. Not a guaranteed timeline or controlled agency comparison.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-neutral-950 px-6 py-16 text-white">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Your site stays your responsibility.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Only WordPress administrators can access Frontman. Keep backups and start with staging for higher-risk work. Some changes have Elementor snapshots or WordPress revisions; there is no universal undo.</p>
			<a href="/how-it-works/" class="copy-link mt-6 inline-block font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">See setup, editing, and live-site safety</a>
			<p class="mt-8 border-t border-white/15 pt-6 text-base leading-7 text-neutral-300">Not using WordPress? <a href="/frameworks/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">Explore Frontman for Next.js, Astro, and Vite</a>. Those integrations produce source changes for developers to review, test, and deploy.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<FinalCTA
		link="https://wordpress.org/plugins/frontman-agentic-ai-editor/"
		title="Your next WordPress update starts with you."
		description="Pick one headline, CTA, or section. Describe the change and inspect the result on your existing site."
		buttonLabel="Get Frontman for WordPress"
	/>
</Layout>

<style>
	section h2 { color: inherit; }
</style>
